{
  "version": 1,
  "comment": "Reviewed word lists for the dialogue audit (daily world slots, Dialogue audit). A line is flagged when it matches a map name (or the stem of a town, city or island name), a landmark noun after a determiner, a terrain noun after a demonstrative, a place phrase or a local-event word, or a sequence phrase that numbers the trainer among a challenge's opponents. Local-event words are matched case-sensitively: the scripts write proper nouns in capitals, so 'No contest at all' is not the CONTEST. A phrase in allowed_phrases (case-sensitive, narrow, each with the reason it reads fine anywhere) is cancelled. Each flagged trainer needs a resolution in reviewed.json. Extend a list here; never silence a trainer. spot_phrases are regexes (case-insensitive) for phrasing that ties a line to its spot without a name; keep them narrow, never a bare 'here'. capital_stems are stems matched only in capitals.",
